# Security & architecture (project)

## Secrets & config

- Never commit API keys, tokens, passwords, or PHI. Use `.env` (gitignored) and `.env.example` with placeholders only.
- Frontend: only `VITE_*` for **non-secret** public config (base URL). No private keys in Vite env.
- No hardcoded credentials, tenant secrets, or internal URLs in source — use env or server-side config.
- Do not log or echo secrets, session tokens, or patient form data in console/errors.

## Exposure

- Sanitize untrusted HTML (DOMPurify in assistant bubbles). Avoid `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization.
- Validate and limit uploads (type, size) client + server. Do not trust `tenantId` or `sessionId` alone for auth in production.
- Generic error messages to users; details server-side only.

## Architecture

- Fetch/network only in `src/services/chatApi.js`. Logic in hooks (`useChatSession`), UI in components.
- One concern per module; no Express/DB code in `src/components/`.
- Prefer extending existing hooks/context over new global state libraries.

## Hooks & memory

- Effects: return cleanup (listeners, timers, intervals, `AbortController`, revoke object URLs).
- Cancel async work when unmounted (`cancelled` flag or abort signal).
- Stable deps: avoid missing `useEffect`/`useCallback` dependencies that cause stale closures or duplicate subscriptions.
- Speech/upload: cancel recognition and revoke `URL.createObjectURL` on unmount or remove.

